With Rugby World Cup (“RWC”) underway the eyes of the world are on our sport. One of the most topical debates across all[ contact] sports[ is] the issue[ of] concussion[ management].
[All] stakeholders will be looking forward to a RWC in which players, medical personnel and team support staff play their part in managing this important aspect of player welfare. Rugby is making significant progress in the[ detection] and management of concussion and it will be important that other professional rugby competitions move to adopt the standards set for[ R]WC 2015. Rugby should not see the[ management] of concussion as a risk at RWC, but an opportunity to demonstrate how far the game has come in recent times.
